{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-15T10:48:17Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-deslop-adjudication-self-suppression","ref_id":"deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine","severity":"P2","finding":"writing the list of indefensible candidates into the spec made the engine suppress them, because any mention in a requirement doc counts as the requirement naming the symbol","decision":"Live count fell from 70 to 58 and suppressed rose from 398 to 410 the moment the adjudication summary landed in the frozen spec; the block says these flags are NOT requirements and the engine reads it as proof that they are. Self-inflicted instance of the prose-suppression false-negative class the LIMITS block already discloses, and it means documenting a finding can erase it","source":"observed 2026-08-15T10:48Z, before/after the adjudication summary was folded into docs/specs/SPEC-DRAFT-spec-deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine.md"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-15T11:31:29Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-deslop-external-call-shape-gaps","ref_id":"deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine","severity":"P3","finding":"The .mjs external-tool exclusion (D3) misses two call shapes: (a) a subprocess call whose command is an expression rather than a string literal, e.g. execFileSync(ghBinOf(opts), [... '--jq' ...]) in hitl-channel.mjs:233 leaks gh's --jq; (b) an argv array built and returned by a helper function rather than a local const, e.g. buildGhArgs() in aai-issues.mjs:235 leaks gh's --state.","decision":"Round-6 validation's independent cross-check (V6-4) found both gaps by reimplementing D2+D3 from scratch and diffing against the engine. Both sites are currently corpus-suppressed (not in the live 58/68 candidate output), so live impact is nil today, and the degrade direction is safe: an unresolvable command word conservatively keeps the flag as a candidate rather than dropping it. Fixing requires engine logic changes, out of scope for this documentation-only remediation pass.","source":"docs/ai/validation/validation-20260815T110436Z-deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine-round6.md section 4 and Findings V6-4"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-15T11:31:29Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-deslop-external-bin-words-closed-list","ref_id":"deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine","severity":"P3","finding":"EXTERNAL_BIN_WORDS (the .sh/.ps1 external-tool recognizer in D3) is a closed, hardcoded 10-binary list (git, gh, cargo, rg, wrangler, tsc, wsl, sed, npm, npx). A binary outside this list, e.g. grep --color=auto, yields --color as a live candidate instead of being excluded.","decision":"Round-6 validation (V6-5) confirmed via an independent fixture. The list is fully disclosed in D3 and is process-based (context-keyed), not a per-flag stoplist, so it does not violate the NO STOPLIST rule -- but it carries the same rot risk a curated list always does. Extending or generalizing it is an engine-logic change, out of scope for this documentation-only remediation pass.","source":"docs/ai/validation/validation-20260815T110436Z-deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine-round6.md Findings V6-5"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-15T11:48:56Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-deslop-all-corpus-specs-only","ref_id":"deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine","severity":"P2","finding":"The --all requirement corpus is docs/specs/** with type: spec only; a flag or config key requested in docs/issues/** or docs/rfc/** is not suppressed and still reports as an unrequested-surface candidate.","decision":"Measured on the live 68-candidate run: 15 of 54 distinct cli-flag symbols (28%) are named in docs/issues or docs/rfc, including --worktree-guard and --worktree-baseline (requested in CHANGE-0125:56) and --pr-config (requested in CHANGE-0096:38). An operator triaging the --all list per the class-4 action would remove a flag a human explicitly asked for, with nothing in the output pointing them at docs/issues/. D2 already treats an intake as a requirement document for --diff; the same reasoning is not applied to --all. NOTE: widening the corpus to docs/issues/** would re-trigger the self-suppression coupling recorded in the CHANGE intake's Adjudication Summary (NB-3) — the 10-row indefensible table currently sits outside the --all corpus only because docs/issues/** is excluded.","source":"docs/ai/reviews/review-20260815T114500Z-deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine.md NB-2"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-15T11:48:58Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-deslop-test014-no-restore-trap","ref_id":"deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine","severity":"P3","finding":"tests/skills/test-aai-deslop.sh:916 TEST-014 runs generate-docs-hub.mjs against the real repo and restores docs/SKILL_CATALOG.html and docs/skill-catalog-data.json from mktemp copies at the end of the function, with no trap.","decision":"A timeout kill from the harness's AAI_TEST_TIMEOUT, a Ctrl-C, or a future return added between the generator invocation and the two cp restores would leave the operator's working tree with a modified tracked catalog file and orphaned mktemp files, showing up as unexplained scope pollution in a pre-PR sweep.","source":"docs/ai/reviews/review-20260815T114500Z-deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine.md NB-7"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-15T14:51:54Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-allocator-misses-wrapped-refs","ref_id":"deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine","severity":"P2","finding":"the allocator's reference-rewrite pass misses a DRAFT basename that is line-wrapped across two comment lines","decision":"CHANGE-0143 made the allocator rewrite DRAFT references in code trees by verbatim basename substitution; a comment wrapping the basename mid-token (deslop-scope-and- / newline) never matches, so a dead SPEC-DRAFT or CHANGE-DRAFT link survives in shipped source. Found by a PR bot on the engine at line 909, exactly the class 0143 was built to kill","source":"PR #260 copilot-pull-request-reviewer, .aai/scripts/deslop-unrequested.mjs:909"}
