{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-18T09:51:54Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-openct-unrdbl-report","ref_id":"followups-cli-hardening","severity":"P2","finding":"generate-factory-report.mjs:616 publishes follow_ups.open_count: 0 for an UNREADABLE ledger (e.g. --decisions a directory), the same 'a bad input reads as good news' shape D2 refuses on the CLI; the file's own oldest_age_days convention two lines down already uses null, never 0, for exactly this degradation","decision":"the honest fix is open_count: registry.unreadable ? null : openFollowUps.length, but Spec-AC-07 of SPEC-DRAFT-spec-followups-cli-hardening.md pins generate-factory-report.mjs byte-unchanged, so it cannot be done inside that scope without breaking a frozen AC","source":"docs/ai/reviews/review-20260818T094328Z-followups-cli-hardening.md NB-3"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-18T09:52:00Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-ledger-isfile-strict","ref_id":"followups-cli-hardening","severity":"P3","finding":"requireReadableLedger (follow-ups.mjs:452) uses !st.isFile(), refusing EVERY non-regular file, not just the directory D2 targets; list --ledger <(cat docs/ai/decisions.jsonl) now exits 2 ledger is not a regular file: /dev/fd/N, where it worked before this change (FIFOs, /dev/stdin, process substitution)","decision":"st.isDirectory() is the honest predicate for the defect being fixed (EACCES/EIO/TOCTOU stay covered by accessSync plus the existing reg.unreadable checks), but Spec-AC-02 of SPEC-DRAFT-spec-followups-cli-hardening.md names fs.statSync(abs).isFile() literally, so relaxing it deviates from a frozen AC","source":"docs/ai/reviews/review-20260818T094328Z-followups-cli-hardening.md NB-5"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-18T11:28:35Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-sync-hash-compare-fails-open","ref_id":"followups-cli-hardening","severity":"P2","finding":"file_content_different in aai-sync.sh treats an unobtainable hash as different, so a transient sha256sum hiccup silently rewrites the target's copilot shim and plants a project-overrides file","decision":"Diagnosed from PR 264's CI-only failure. Under set -o pipefail a failed fork in the sha256sum awk pipeline flips the comparison to different; at aai-sync.sh:445 that switches the copilot-instructions shim from copy_replace into the merge branch, which mutates the tree. Simulating one transient failure on Linux reproduced the reported symptom byte for byte. The fix is to fail closed: treat an unobtainable hash as not different, or read the hash without a pipefail-sensitive pipeline","source":"diagnosis of PR 264 skill-suite failure on 2d122b4, aai-sync.sh lines 142-173 and 445"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-18T11:28:35Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-idempotence-assert-no-diff","ref_id":"followups-cli-hardening","severity":"P3","finding":"the core-sync idempotence assertion discards both sync logs and prints no diff, so a rare failure costs a full investigation to reproduce","decision":"test-aai-layer-profiles.sh TEST-004 sends both sync runs to /dev/null and fails with a bare message. The sync's own MERGE preserved project overrides line would have named the cause immediately. Printing the snapshot diff on failure is a few lines and belongs regardless of the underlying cause","source":"diagnosis of PR 264, tests/skills/test-aai-layer-profiles.sh lines 281-285"}
