{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-19T00:56:27Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-docnumbering-t013-writes-real-tree","ref_id":"deslop-corpus-honesty","severity":"P2","finding":"tests/skills/test-aai-doc-numbering.sh TEST-013 runs generate-docs-index.mjs against PROJECT_ROOT and rewrites docs/INDEX.md in whatever tree it runs in","decision":"a suite that mutates the real repository cannot be run safely during validation or remediation, so the surface it covers gets skipped exactly when it matters; this is the second such suite found in one day, after test-aai-docs-audit.sh","source":"remediation of validation round 6, deslop-corpus-honesty, 2026-08-19; observed rewriting docs/INDEX.md in every scratchpad copy it ran in"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-19T06:25:07Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-docnumbering-logfail-aborts-suite","ref_id":"deslop-corpus-honesty","severity":"P2","finding":"log_fail in tests/skills/test-aai-doc-numbering.sh calls exit 1, so the first failed assertion aborts the whole suite and every later arm silently never runs","decision":"measured 2026-08-19: while docs-audit is NEEDS-TRIAGE the suite aborts at TEST-013 and TEST-014 onward never execute, so a suite that appears to cover doc numbering currently reports on almost nothing, and its own coverage loss is invisible in the output","source":"validation round 7 of deslop-corpus-honesty, harness_note (b); reproduced in a scratchpad copy"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-19T06:25:07Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-mutation-rig-copies-whole-tree","ref_id":"deslop-corpus-honesty","severity":"P3","finding":"mutation testing has no rig, so each trial rsyncs the whole 119 MB tree and re-runs a full suite; nine trials plus a fixture battery cost one validation round five and a half hours","decision":"mutation proof is the only technique that has caught any of the eight could-not-fail defects found on this ride, and its cost is what makes roles skip it or run out of budget before the verdict-gating checks; a shared read-only base plus an overlay would make it routine","source":"validation round 7 of deslop-corpus-honesty, harness_note (a), 2026-08-19: 19523 s wall, standing set never reached"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-19T06:29:15Z","actor":"remediation","type":"process_finding","ref_id":"deslop-corpus-honesty","severity":"P2","finding":"correction to fu-docnumbering-t013-writes-real-tree: its reproduction note was inaccurate","detail":"The original follow-up (2026-08-19T00:56:27Z) claimed TEST-013 was \"observed rewriting docs/INDEX.md in every scratchpad copy it ran in\". That observation is wrong. Validation round 7 showed that on this tree TEST-013 aborts at its own `assert_contains ... CLEAN` docs-audit precondition before it ever reaches generate-docs-index.mjs, so tests/skills/test-aai-doc-numbering.sh does not currently rewrite docs/INDEX.md in any tree. The hazard itself stands and the item stays open at P2: generate-docs-index.mjs does write (proven on a scratchpad copy, docs/INDEX.md sha 0f3bd66 -> f50ced6), and TEST-013 does invoke it against PROJECT_ROOT, so the suite arms itself the moment docs-audit reports CLEAN. Treat the item as a latent real-tree write hazard, not an observed one; the do-not-run-against-the-real-tree guidance is unchanged.","relates_to":"fu-docnumbering-t013-writes-real-tree","source":"validation round 7, deslop-corpus-honesty; corrected by remediation round 7 (R-17)"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-19T07:54:49Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-round7-report-never-written","ref_id":"deslop-corpus-honesty","severity":"P3","finding":"validation round 7 returned a full verdict in its subagent record but never wrote its report to docs/ai/validation, so the on-disk evidence trail jumps round6 to round8","decision":"the findings that drove two remediations exist only in conversation prose; a reader auditing this ride from the repository alone cannot reconstruct why those changes were made","source":"delta code review NB-4, 2026-08-19; ls docs/ai/validation shows no round7 file"}
{"v": 1, "ts": "2026-08-19T08:31:00Z", "actor": "remediation", "type": "process_finding", "ref_id": "deslop-corpus-honesty", "severity": "P2", "finding": "correction to the R-16 justification for the dangling symlink added to TEST-026's empty-by-filter (d3) fixture: the fixture is fine, the reason recorded for it was wrong", "detail": "R-16 added `ln -s /nonexistent/BROKEN3.md` to the d3 fixture in tests/skills/test-aai-deslop.sh and recorded it as PROVEN load-bearing by a blind control - the claim being that the pre-symlink, draft-only fixture could not catch the guard-restoration regression (restoring `&& !result.corpus.empty` to renderJson's excludedBlock selection) and that only the added unreadable member made the pin bite. The delta code review (NB-2) measured otherwise, and remediation round 8 re-measured it independently on a scratchpad copy: with the guard restored and NO symlink present, the draft-only fixture already fails TWO clauses of the d3 node_check - `c.excluded.draft === 1` reads 0 (the zero-literal fall-through) and `c.examined === c.count + sum` reads 1 vs 0. The unmutated control on the same fixture passes both. The R-16 'blind' control therefore did not exercise the regression the pin guards; it used a bespoke narrowed mutation. DISPOSITION: the symlink STAYS - `empty by filter AND carrying an unreadable member` is a distinct, real corpus shape and the added coverage is genuine - but it is kept for coverage, not because the fixture could not otherwise bite. The original R-16 record and the fixture are left unedited; the overstating comment block in the suite (the B-4 note) is corrected in place by this same round.", "relates_to": "tests/skills/test-aai-deslop.sh test_026_document_accounting_balances (d3 fixture)", "source": "delta code review NB-2, 2026-08-19; re-measured by remediation round 8 on a scratchpad copy (engine_guard_regression.mjs vs pristine engine over a draft-only, symlink-free fixture)"}
