{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-20T20:30:18Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-iso-exec-script-basename-only","ref_id":"suites-run-in-a-disposable-worktree","severity":"P3","finding":"aai_iso_exec_script recognises a shell interpreter by basename only, so 'env bash tests/skills/test-framework.sh' or 'nohup bash ...' treats env/nohup as the executed script and the framework opt-out does not apply","decision":"the framework would then be isolated and its run ledger discarded with the disposable checkout; the direction is fail-toward-isolation and never a bypass, and the canonical invocations in AGENTS.md are unaffected, so it is a limit worth naming rather than a defect worth blocking on","source":"self-reported residual by the remediation that wrote the fix, 2026-08-20; deliberately left unfiled by that agent because main was clean and it had no commit authorisation"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-20T20:50:49Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up_status","id":"fu-deslop-test014-no-restore-trap","status":"done","resolved_by":"CHANGE-0151","source":"Verified in main at 6d5e320: tests/skills/test-aai-deslop.sh:950-1009 test_014_description_surfaces_and_catalog_idempotence no longer writes PROJECT_ROOT at all. The in-place regeneration and the two untrapped cp restores are deleted; generate-docs-hub.mjs now runs with cwd set to a new_fixture mirror (hub) holding copies of .claude and .aai/SKILL_ prompt files, and writes its two outputs there. PROJECT_ROOT is only READ, at lines 965-966, to hash the committed artifacts for the drift compare. /usr/bin/grep -n SKILL_CATALOG tests/skills/test-aai-deslop.sh returns 8 hits, none of them a cp or a restore. There is nothing left to restore, so the missing trap has no subject."}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-20T20:50:59Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up_status","id":"fu-docnumbering-t013-writes-real-tree","status":"done","resolved_by":"CHANGE-0151","source":"Verified in main at 6d5e320: tests/skills/test-aai-doc-numbering.sh:676-692 test_013_regression runs generate-docs-index.mjs twice with cwd set to a repo-index-mirror directory built by cp -R of PROJECT_ROOT/docs, snapshots and diffs the mirror copy of docs/INDEX.md, then rm -rf's the mirror. The only PROJECT_ROOT invocation left in the arm is docs-audit.mjs --check --strict --no-event, which is read-only (--no-event suppresses the EVENTS append). No generate-docs-index.mjs call with cwd PROJECT_ROOT remains anywhere in the suite, so the arm cannot rewrite the tracked docs/INDEX.md in whatever tree it runs in."}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-20T20:50:59Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up_status","id":"fu-speclint-t011-writes-real-tree","status":"done","resolved_by":"CHANGE-0151","source":"Verified in main at 6d5e320: tests/skills/test-aai-spec-lint.sh:449-461 test_011_seam_survival regenerates the index twice with cwd set to a mktemp idx-mirror holding a cp -R of PROJECT_ROOT/docs, hashes the mirror's docs/INDEX.md, then rm -rf's it. /usr/bin/grep -n generate-docs-index tests/skills/test-aai-spec-lint.sh returns exactly the two mirror invocations at lines 454 and 456 and no PROJECT_ROOT call. The tests/skills/test-aai-delta-stage2.sh symptom was inherited purely by invoking this suite, so it disappears with the source write."}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-20T20:52:46Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-spec-closes-claim-unverified","ref_id":"registry-audit-20260820","severity":"P2","finding":"a spec's 'Registry items closed by this scope' line is never checked against the ledger, so a frozen document can claim closures that never happened","decision":"measured 2026-08-20: SPEC-0137 named 3 items closed and 0 of those 3 were; CHANGE-0146 named 4 and 2 were. tests/skills/test-aai-deslop.sh test_030 already performs exactly this check for one scope, so the pattern exists and is simply not a general close-ceremony gate; a generic arm would have caught all three misses","source":"registry audit 2026-08-20, 85 open items reviewed against current main"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-20T20:52:46Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-adhoc-probes-unisolated-report-only","ref_id":"registry-audit-20260820","severity":"P2","finding":"aai-run-tests.sh isolates suite runs only, by design, so every generator, build, node one-liner and probe a role runs through the canonical wrapper executes in the shipping tree with a guard that cannot fail the run","decision":"measured: a helper script through the canonical wrapper printed toplevel and pwd as the shipping repo on branch main; this is the surface the P1 fu-subagent-probe-hits-real-repo actually names, and worktree isolation does not cover it","source":"registry audit 2026-08-20; probe run through .aai/scripts/aai-run-tests.sh, PROBE-TOPLEVEL and PROBE-HEAD both the live repo"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-20T20:52:46Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"process_finding","ref_id":"registry-audit-20260820","finding":"fu-followups-json-truncated-on-pipe has crossed from latent to live. It was filed on 2026-08-19 with the note that the ledger measured 56549 bytes and the defect did not bite yet. Measured today: the ledger is 88066 bytes, `follow-ups.mjs list --json` piped into a parser yields exactly 65536 bytes and JSON.parse fails at position 65522. Every caller that pipes the registry is now silently reading a truncated ledger.","decision":"Treat as P2-now-biting rather than P2-latent; the item cannot be re-severed in an append-only ledger, so this record carries the escalation. Any count quoted from a piped read after 2026-08-20 is suspect; redirect to a file and read the file. The prediction in the original filing - that it would surprise someone later - was right within one day.","source":"registry audit 2026-08-20"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-20T21:29:44Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-cli-exit-truncates-pipe-sweep","ref_id":"cli-output-survives-a-pipe","severity":"P2","finding":"41 of the .aai/scripts/*.mjs CLIs still print with console.log and then call process.exit, the exact shape that truncated follow-ups.mjs list --json at 65536 bytes on a pipe; docs-audit.mjs (23 logs), test-canon.mjs (28), docs-canon.mjs (23) and metrics-flush.mjs (15) are the largest payloads","decision":"cli-output-survives-a-pipe deliberately fixed ONE file; a repo-wide sweep needs its own scope, its own per-CLI exit-code proof and its own regression pins, and doing it inside that ride would have made the diff unreviewable","source":"docs/specs/SPEC-DRAFT-spec-cli-output-survives-a-pipe.md D7"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-20T22:13:45Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-followups-dead-return-usageerror","ref_id":"cli-output-survives-a-pipe","severity":"P3","finding":"follow-ups.mjs:517 has an unreachable return; after a usageError() call that can no longer return","decision":"usageError now throws an ExitSignal, so the trailing return is dead code that misleads a reader into thinking the catch arm can fall through; it was dead before this change too (validation round-1 F4)","source":"docs/ai/validation/validation-20260820T213357Z-cli-output-survives-a-pipe-round1.md F4; .aai/scripts/follow-ups.mjs:516-517"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-20T22:13:53Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-pipeguard-nonepipe-arm-unproven","ref_id":"cli-output-survives-a-pipe","severity":"P3","finding":"installPipeGuard's non-EPIPE re-throw arm is read-verified only, never executed by any test","decision":"/dev/full is absent on macOS, so no arm produces a non-EPIPE stream error (ENOSPC); the branch that must re-throw rather than exit is therefore unproved at runtime and a later edit could silently turn a real write failure into exit 0","source":"docs/ai/validation/validation-20260820T213357Z-cli-output-survives-a-pipe-round1.md attack 18; .aai/scripts/follow-ups.mjs:365-373"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-20T22:14:00Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-pipe-exit-contract-windows-untested","ref_id":"cli-output-survives-a-pipe","severity":"P3","finding":"the throw-based exit contract and the EPIPE guard in follow-ups.mjs were never measured on Windows","decision":"pipe-write synchrony and EPIPE semantics are platform-dependent in Node; every measurement in this ride ran on macOS and in a Linux container, so the Windows behaviour of the flush-before-exit path is an untested assumption","source":"docs/ai/validation/validation-20260820T213357Z-cli-output-survives-a-pipe-round1.md residual risks"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-21T03:33:02Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-orchestrator-mutated-real-file","ref_id":"cli-output-survives-a-pipe","severity":"P2","finding":"the orchestrator ran a bite-proof mutation against the tracked suite file instead of a copy, and the first restore attempt silently failed on a mis-anchored sed pattern","decision":"every role dispatch this week forbids exactly this, and the near-miss was shipping a test with a shrunken fixture that cannot fail, inside a ride about assertions that cannot fail; the restore also had no verification step until one was added by hand afterwards","source":"2026-08-21 03:35Z; mutation applied to tests/skills/test-aai-follow-ups.sh in place, detected by git diff --stat, reversed and re-verified (396 insertions 0 deletions, suite green, no t022big 5 artefact)"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-21T03:53:42Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-docsaudit-t003-utc-date-bomb","ref_id":"cli-output-survives-a-pipe","severity":"P1","finding":"test-aai-docs-audit TEST-003 strips only the leading Generated line before comparing the regenerated docs/INDEX.md with the committed one, but the generated file carries a second dated line 'Today (UTC): <date>', so the committed INDEX goes stale at every UTC midnight and the arm goes red until someone regenerates it","decision":"a suite that turns red once a day for a reason unrelated to any change trains everyone to read its failure as noise, which is how a real failure gets waved through; proven on a pristine detached-HEAD checkout with zero ride changes, and observed live at 03:35Z when the committed INDEX still said 2026-08-20","source":"round-2 validation of cli-output-survives-a-pipe, 2026-08-21; reported as filed by that round and by the orchestrator and in fact never filed until now — third recurrence of fu-suggested-ids-read-as-filed"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-21T03:53:57Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-test021c-precondition-unasserted","ref_id":"cli-output-survives-a-pipe","severity":"P2","finding":"TEST-021(c) never asserts its own precondition that the reader is gone before the write, so the arm reaches the same observable with the guard removed and an open reader","decision":"measured 10 of 10 both ways, so the arm can go green without ever invoking installPipeGuard; it is the only arm holding the load-bearing half of the EPIPE guard, and it does not hold it","source":"code review NB-1, cli-output-survives-a-pipe, 2026-08-21"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-21T04:30:21Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-main-push-conflicts-open-pr","ref_id":"cli-output-survives-a-pipe","severity":"P2","finding":"the orchestrator pushed a commit to main that regenerated docs/INDEX.md while a PR shipping the same generated file was open, turning that PR CONFLICTING","decision":"fourth instance in two days of writing to a tree something else depends on (parallel roles, a merge mid-framework-run, a commit mid-run, now a push mid-PR); each cost a rerun, and the shared generated files docs/INDEX.md, overview.* and factory-report.* make it near-certain whenever a doc lands on main during an open PR","source":"2026-08-21 04:28Z; PR 268 went CONFLICTING after main commit 8980a07, resolved by merging main into the branch and regenerating the index"}
